OL,3,GNEWSACider farms report 'lighter' apple
OL,4,Acrops in heat
OL,5,
OL,6,FCider producers across the South West
OL,7,Fhave said the hot, dry weather has
OL,8,Fmeant their apples have been smaller
OL,9,Fand their crops "exceptionally
OL,10,Flighter".
OL,12,FAlison McIlwraith, cider farm owner in
OL,13,FOkehampton, said her business expected
OL,14,Fto produce 10% of the cider this year
OL,15,Fthat they made last, after the dry
OL,16,Fsummer following a wet spring had
OL,17,Fimpacted the crop.
OL,23,APub: 20-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,345,340,200,160,0,100
